# M-31: SQL Agent FAISS/.pkl embedding artifacts are large, binary, and
# churn as a whole file on every rebuild (not line-diffable) -- exactly
# what Git LFS exists for. Scoped specifically to backend/sql_agent's two
# versioned embedding directories (5.5 and 6.0), NOT every .pkl/.faiss file
# in the repository, so unrelated binary files elsewhere are unaffected.
#
# This file only prepares LFS tracking for files added/changed AFTER it
# takes effect -- the files currently tracked in these directories were
# committed as regular Git blobs before this change and remain so until a
# separate, explicit history-migration step (`git lfs migrate import`) is
# run. See doc/runbooks/ (or the M-31 report) for that step's exact command
# and its consequences -- it was deliberately NOT run as part of this change.
backend/sql_agent/embeddings_5.5/*.faiss filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
backend/sql_agent/embeddings_5.5/*.pkl   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
backend/sql_agent/embeddings_6.0/*.faiss filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
backend/sql_agent/embeddings_6.0/*.pkl   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
